      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 11. नैर्झर-निर्झरसम्बन्धि of a spring. उचित proper. विद्याङ्गना",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "—विद्या एव अङ्गना ( प्रशस्तानि अङ्गानि यस्याः सा; fr. अङ्ग+न ) a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "beautiful woman. रत्यै—for deriving pleasure which is usually",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "had from woman’s society. The dat. is तादर्थ्ये—Mr. Telang who",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "reads रत्येव supposes that र might be a mislection for स ( येषां",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "विद्यैव सती अङ्गना ). सेवाअलिः—the bow of obeisance.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 12. त्रिलोकीसरित्—the Ganges, so called because it flows",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "through the three worlds, स्वर्, मृत्यु, and पाताल. नीवि-the tie-knot",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "of a woman’s under-garment and sometimes the garment itself.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "कल्पयन्ती० providing, supplying; for वृत्ति comp. the preceding",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "sloka. दुःखासिकानाम्—trying or painful circumstances; or दुःखम-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "सिका इव poignant pain (lit. misery cutting like a poniard ). For",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "a similar idea cf. दीना दीनमुखैः &c. sl. 22. supra.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 13. तीव्रातितीव्रं तपः—is the same to an ascetic as उद्यानेषु",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "०विधि to ordinary mortals. The two expressions are here identifi-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "ed and mean–to the ascetic penance is like a garden-party. Some",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "take the two expressions separately, but then there is hardly",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "any propriety of garden parties in the case of a saint. अमितं",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "भिक्षाटनं मण्डनम्—( where) a roaming for alms, not measured, i. e.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "at one’s will, is a glory. हन्त is here used खेदे, to show the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "poet’s regret at wise men staying elsewhere, and not in Benares.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 14. The first line and half of the second contain the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "replies of gate-keepers or guards to supposed questions. समयः—",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "the proper time. रहस्यं—He ( the master ) is now engaged in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "confidential matters; or as Mr. Telang takes it-now he is in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "private. द्रक्ष्यसि—द्रक्ष्यति v. l. does not make good sense. दौवारिक-",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "( fr. द्वार+ठक् ) a door-keeper. अपरुषं—may be taken as a",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "separate word or as part of the preceding compound word.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "निःसीमं &c.—निःसीमं शर्म प्रददातीति । conferring unbounded",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "happiness.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 15. बलवति-breaks the symmetry as this is the only noun",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "having an adj. to quilify it. तृणे वा स्त्रैणे वा—स्त्रैण is used here more",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "for the sake of alliteration than as being the recognised opposite",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
